# DERIVED fixture, one literal away from run-with-dormancy.nq: its
# sw:dormancyReason reads "automatic" rather than "operator-hold". Every other
# byte of the 115 quads is that file's, which is emitter output copied from
# prober/state/task-4-e2e/run-2.nq. So this is NOT a captured run of its own,
# and the one edit is named here rather than left for a reader to diff.
#
# It exists because "automatic" had no loadable fixture at all. The only
# committed file carrying that value is run-measures-and-declares-dormant.nq,
# which exists to be REFUSED by web/load_run.py, so the sentence this page
# prints for a machine relegation was unit-tested against a hand-built
# dataclass and had never been rendered through a real store. That is the case
# a stranger meets in production far more often than the operator-hold case:
# an operator hold is one person's decision about one endpoint, and the
# automatic path is what the policy does to every endpoint that costs more
# than the ceiling while answering nothing, twice in a row.
#
# WHY THE EDIT IS SOUND. The dormancy group's shape does not depend on the
# reason: prober/src/emit.rs writes sw:dormantEndpoint, sw:dormancyReason and
# sw:dormantSince for either value, and prober/src/dormancy.rs decides which
# word goes in. The sw:dormantSince here is 2026-08-27T09:30:00Z, which the
# emitter took from the state file, and for an automatic relegation that is the
# instant of the sweep that recorded the second strike rather than the instant
# an operator typed a command. Nothing in web/ reads it, and both readings are
# an instant in the past, so the value stands unchanged.
#
# 115 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-27T10:00:00Z), the same
# instant and the same trio as run-with-dormancy.nq. The two files therefore
# cannot be loaded into one store: they are two spellings of one run, not two
# runs, and a store holding both would hold one run graph saying the reason is
# both words. Load this one BESIDE run-with-samples.nq, which is what
# conftest's store_dormant_automatic does.
